hed forward, taking a gigantic crag; and that one possessed of great strength, hurled it at the Raksasa. And thereat Kumbha \"severed that crag with five shafts discharged (from his bow).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5949468809911ac35e42e5ec0ecc77f8def379860d1eee852d0303579db45c33","compact":"55f8d18dd141387b2ac079e583f92e34c6f11ee5231056bcc2e9db44aa8e4b52","nasal":"584e20f914ee60ebba02f87939df0de1084b52a93563f972b999ab53c338b325"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":10,"english":"Mainda, seeing his brother, broken in mighty encounter, furiously rushed forward, taking a gigantic crag; and that one possessed of great strength, hurled it at the Raksasa. And thereat Kumbha \"severed that crag with five shafts discharged (from his bow).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.894,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8410c6c341c2afe4565d82aa30821d0f560c0b8a454614e6493f07a2a9a4a796","compact":"028fefa4446774b9c61be700d4c4d235c92956a4dbb0746d9fdea7ba7df886c9","nasal":"8f99a14c13ee1a646ff263553c13092b7cf110aa044dd3796da539ebc221819c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":11,"english":"Then aiming other fair-headed arrows resembling venomous snakes, that exceedingly energetic one smote Dvivida's elder brother in the chest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9