ighty lords of monkey, with showers of shafts, even as a crag obstruct the course of a current.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-51"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"742ef0a3312c36b5196175eb7fd3da92cc2f4251108552f6d7d7f848ed110c39","compact":"f9d4ebf5dc7b704edb143285bacdfd3f6eeccb1587e6e58923457c224930a627","nasal":"51d0dd924055261146f3b2ae375e1c2f617319107ae9f4209bfa2cc7a35f5951"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":28,"english":"Even the great deep cannot see his own shores, those high-souled lord of monkeys, coming within the range of his arrows, could not even see.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.574,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-52"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ef4ca5038ff52e19eb60dbbddf0f9e75de96032aad9fb4e6ab4cd47d2cfa227f","compact":"6a97fbdc2b9677600525a801736fa43131cd7d7dbe454c65da6e6ba1a4afef57","nasal":"81953b75bc175cbfb029c46d262a6f50420ba4251d957862cbb8fccdd0d410bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":29,"english":"Seeing those monkeys sore distressed by the shafts, the king of the monkeys, Sugrīva, in that conflict taking his brother's son on his back, rushed against the son of Kumbhakarna, even as a powerful lion rush at an elephant ranging on the slopes of a mountain.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-53"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e6c52753e9fffea0dc670a2b4c039c0ba413778a82573d276158db044484fccd","compact":"bc8445260ae