t mightier father. As mental anguish does not dog one that has controlled his senses, the celestials cannot cope in conflict with you alone, O repressor of foes, O of mighty arms, bearing your dart in your hand. O you of high intelligence, put forth your prowess! and do you also witness my work.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d19bf50a0b39f55336bbc2d1291c5cf11543396eea15c559d7520a6683d46bfa","compact":"880594510ec6b0176e0d65cba65d257c2d3217f28dd835bf2f6e7034c6936a8d","nasal":"5eeb0993b331378495fe03b286725003fa6691774f2bfa0c3fd4fa99316ba218"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":38,"english":"O elder brother of Nikumbha, marvellous are your might and the force of yourself as well as the modesty and prowess that are your and Ravana's. And, o you equal to Prahrada or Vall or the slayer of Vặtra or Varuņa or Kuvera! You alone walk in the wake of you yet mightier father. As mental anguish does not dog one that has controlled his senses, the celestials cannot cope in conflict with you alone, O repressor of foes, O of mighty arms, bearing your dart in your hand. O you of high intelligence, put forth your prowess! and do you also witness my work.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0704e6c3b415f98448ca6066b77d580c025dd8151708653e89bb0463af6c066a","compact":"90855fb96dcc559bc5c5c15e0a176dcc31b2127d1664a088402e1aff7c886a3d","nasal":"90855fb96dcc559bc5c5c15e0a176dcc31b2127d1664a088402e1aff7c886a3d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":39,"english":"O elder brother of Nikumbha, marvellous are your might and the force of yourself as well as the modesty and prowess that are your and Ravana's. And, o you equal to Prahrada or Vall or the slayer of Vặtra or Varuņa or Kuvera! You alone walk in the wake of you yet mightier father. As mental anguish does not dog one that has controlled his senses, the celestials cannot cope in conflict with you alone, O repressor of foes, O of mighty arms, bearing your dart in your hand. O you of high intelligence, put forth your prowess! and do you also witness my work.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dd5b3427d8924b09021ad5eaa14174991f9abf3170f220beb951893f1b92e463","compact":"3e393dad75878494e0cf7405fd31938a6b0457a90bce0fb55112241d29c9a41c","nasal":"1cf9da96fe8d81475011e433a3d9976645d51a775975aa2cb1921cf8e1906285"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-40","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":40,"english":"It is only by virtue of the boon he has received, that your uncle can bear the deities and the Dānavas. But Kumbhakarņa cop with the immortals and Asuras by means of his native might. And in the bow equal to Indrajit himself and in power equal to Rāvana, you now in might and energy are the foremost of Räkşasas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-59"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a8e475f2ec1f9a4ee443875b5d13b2c4d8e8b2bef114666bc82c5225f62817c","compact":"5a85cb6899d308ff4a9ff1fc0f4b2d0701411b53c3ac02f98e6c2b6d672009a2","nasal":"3475964771875d9a228d11985d873eec72cc88b6da0d64970c8d0f37f87136d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":41,"english":"It is only by virtue of the boon he has received, that your uncle can bear the deities and the Dānavas. But Kumbhakarņa cop with the immortals and Asuras by means of his native might. And in the bow equal to Indrajit himself and in power equal to Rāvana, you now in might and energy are the foremost of Räkşasas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-59"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7efc56756e235888a0de5221fd3d51bdcb706722c3b1891dd2a981e133a9a937","compact":"11da613efca2e5d46b09c5692b9e27737eb7a10cffcd06db9588cd2d7e78da27","nasal":"0adb416930a89d9c046b323bae6ee47af1861c5b50b0a0366deca981ab2e92d4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":42,"english":"Today let all creatures witness the mighty and wonderful encounter in conflict between you and me, like to the meeting of Śakra and Sambara.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-60"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06a20cd50767cbbd525ed45cbf322a4af9846814a3f9657e061e4902df7ee1ee","compact":"3c476c1a041fe2f6a7e97f1918166b236c5a54c3f98730779bc740242f1fde81","nasal":"89436c56681aad81a027c57484fbd42edec76a5ca7e4a850b8661d1f5a656adf"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":43,"english":"Unparalleled is the feat you have performed; and you have displayed your skill in weapons. And heroic monkeys endowed with dreadful vigour, have been brought down by you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-61"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0033d33ebc91aec11a18c8501011f1d425c2c44f894d80af88ab760431a81ae","compact":"f425f90011cbc5e0009b525f58b8878ef0ee0674f49cdfbf9cb6e26653fc3607","nasal":"558caabb6cd808f9f513ba6225acac4fd7839287afe8ea40015391a99e001abf"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":44,"english":"O hero it is only because of the apprehension* of censure of the people that I do not slay you who are fatigued in consequence of the acts that you have performed. And reposing from fight, do you see my strength! *i.e. Lest people should censure me, saying, Sugrīva slew Kumbha when he was fatigued in fight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.705,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-62"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063044","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e08e69521a77af8009c87e525db246789849722f7f0a5b8e89c7b29fd717517","compact":"f7f6ed5ccf24dce831c8f6a4cc41a75feec8913ba58b702b632998a1da347cf9","nasal":"ac5934dded9445f694a7502d1a81faa4713ee8d40616623607d2fe5138883f2f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-45","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":45,"english":"Being thus honoured (by Sugrīva) with fair speech, (Kumbha) flamed up like a flame into which oblations have been poured.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-63"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063045","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4f11743ab4495e42f5ca11f6d60bff97e105dcb5450a04ed995956018004c46","compact":"f4172d1a5b64adb4321aad2f81685fcc7d4bd93a18a536279557fd24eaf3308d","nasal":"f4172d1a5b64adb4321aad2f81685fcc7d4bd93a18a536279557fd24eaf3308d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-46","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":46,"english":"Then springing up, and bringing Sugriva down, Kumbha, transported with wrath dealt a blow on his chest, like to the levin.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-67"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063046","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad1d3285fee626e2df55a2117303f038bc100b33233fdc8bad285d53d795dd2e","compact":"e1dedd1ccf50586b5008545681c8ff2d616730d39d8702ec5e2d4fedfdee1fa8","nasal":"c84880e632a5dae977294c17e50c9b41e958e8b26f9e56e5c8df56181a8c1b4b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-47","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":47,"english":"Thereat his skin was rent, and blood began to gush out, and the impetus of that blow broke Sugriva's bones.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.631,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-68"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063047","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86343d869bb7b2555607dd2bdf050cfc97c296afde496fa59d5285fc1d9efa7d","compact":"bcb60302ce6111d506a7a7f746366c01f61ec1957de9b580f0efa9b44dd1d03b","nasal":"cbd94534c1cf735780f8521bb6191371c730553cb2bf8cdd633528756d981eb4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-48","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":48,"english":"The vehemence (of the blow) caused a great fire to blaze up at that spot, even as the thunderbolt smiting the mountain Meru, make place blazed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.444,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-69"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063048","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f98d95ebaf4442045e20a79b2431d8b937390419d75b2cd664d8e2e7ec8bb6f","compact":"e85c05566dc11bb1d9f739f1860d3672764430156a9a67b192c9a8419491006c","nasal":"e85c05566dc11bb1d9f739f1860d3672764430156a9a67b192c9a8419491006c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-49","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":49,"english":"The mighty Sugrīva foremost of monkeys-sorely handled by him, fastened his fingers into a box resembling the thunder-bolt, and furnished with all the effulgence of the solar disc having a thousand rays.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-70"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063049","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6763f524015cf0f93b208d8fdfe6015637a440d1cccf26a37df8e37c857c1434","compact":"ef39aebd32b1a1cdf3b8904ce25342726b181d40b74763b0f49b95f60fa4d468","nasal":"ef39aebd32b1a1cdf3b8904ce25342726b181d40b74763b0f49b95f60fa4d468"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-50","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":50,"english":"Then that powerful one made that blow descend right on on Kumbha's breast. And agonised with that stroke, Kumbha reft of his senses, dropped like to a fire that has lost its brightness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.492,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-71"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063050","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"61cbd6ff0e13339b3a1e7f09f193c1de93a188cc9e41bbc51fe4e82ed363e1fc","compact":"c9322efbfc37a15fa7a2207f6c06a46cbe2570c92a72dbcd7a392bd5df0e2cf1","nasal":"271028881d599f6a8d86b810b47129990b1465c56c4700d176775f852f14c00b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-51","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":51,"english":"And overpowered by that blow, the Rākṣasa anon dropped down, like to the bright Lohitānga dropping from the firmament urged on by Destiny.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-72"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063051","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c0f8b51d852422707a60d19d7ac0e82d700f7ef564d754215e1e84f8ee06f7aa","compact":"3314e8b35fe3ddaaa81c9047663e19d8a63f0604ec6d0902a9c116935d521834","nasal":"4f5ee738a1788e037346b486dcb28fe9237d372ba3547f56bc2d97fbc4d222ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-52","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":52,"english":"The aspect of the falling Kumbha with his breast broken by the blow, appeared like that of the Sun routed by Rudra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-73"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063052","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a01ff879fafdc3f75a8dd95b9a586a6134ee9e660eefc8c61155ea85cc9ace5a","compact":"420ea094f9d41536f06d83021add0a9e8cc111ef981e4f3ca1b369e264c49458","nasal":"5be638249a2ef76e8831a04fb61697a8daac63357bf4465287c16c4689a843c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-63-53","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":63,"verse":53,"english":"On his being slain, in encounter, by the foremost of monkeys endowed with terrific strength, the earth with her hills and woods, shook; and a mighty fear took possession of the Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-76-74"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6063053","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e8f6b4aabe7e597379f6a59dce8bdadebcfc575da7e86e71c6cd26f8caad6af","compact":"58fc1874877fa2dd221abb743c9f36d60739d8f93e3a99337a276ead425b0ae9","nasal":"58fc1874877fa2dd221abb743c9f36d60739d8f93e3a99337a276ead425b0ae9"}}]
